lt_kirciai.tsv    - Lithuanian stress dictionary (word, vowel group index, pitch accent mark,
                    optional IPA vowel group index where espeak-ng splits a diphthong).
lt_raides.tsv     - letter names espeak-ng gets wrong when a word is spelled out
                    (own work of Reginutė, GPL-3.0-only).
lt_kreipiniai.tsv - nouns that occur as direct address, for the vocative accent rule
                    (own work of Reginutė, GPL-3.0-only).

lt_kirciai.tsv is CC-BY-4.0 AND GPL-3.0-only. Its entries come from two CC-BY-4.0 sources:
  https://huggingface.co/datasets/meldynamics/liepa-tts   LIEPA corpus annotation (Vilnius University)
  https://github.com/svogunas/g2p-lt-lexicon               pronunciation lexicon (Arunas Smaliukas)
Reginutė's build script (sudaryk_zodyna.py) merges them, and its manual corrections
are Reginutė's own work, GPL-3.0-only like the rest of Reginutė's code.

Copied from Reginutė (Robertas Tarasevičius) at commit 328d98dc236daa806ef8d85f9818cda3d67303ad:
  https://github.com/RobertasTa/reginute/tree/328d98dc236daa806ef8d85f9818cda3d67303ad
The three files are byte-identical to lt_kirciai.tsv, lt_raides.tsv and lt_kreipiniai.tsv there.

COPYING is the GPL version 3 text, byte-identical to LICENSE in Reginutė.

LICENSE is the attribution notice for the two CC-BY-4.0 sources, followed by the
CC-BY-4.0 text. Robertas Tarasevičius wrote it for his copy of these files in
OHF-Voice/piper1-gpl (src/piper/lithuanian/LICENSE, added in commit
1f8f445294064ca3a388aba3732601cd9ff3c804). The vendored file is byte-identical to it.
Reginutė itself has no such notice.
